{'symbol': 'BA', 'date': '2020-05-02 04:30:00', 'title': 'Ryanair grounds most flights until July, says reviewing growth plans', 'text': "RYANAIR HOLDINGS PLC – COVID-19 MARKET UPDATE.PLANS FOR A LIKELY RETURN TO SERVICES IN Q2.EXPECTS TO OPERATE LESS THAN 1% OF ITS SCHEDULED FLYING PROGRAM IN APR, MAY & JUNE 2020.EU LEVEL PLAYING FIELD WILL BE DISTORTED BY COMPETING AGAINST LEGACY AIRLINES WHO ARE RECEIVING OVER EUR 30 BILLION OF STATE AI.RYANAIR EXPECTS TO OPERATE LESS THAN 1% OF ITS SCHEDULED FLYING PROGRAM IN APR, MAY & JUNE 2020.3,000 JOB CUTS AND PAY CUTS - CONSULTATIONS.RYANAIR EXPECTS TO OPERATE LESS THAN 1% OF ITS SCHEDULED FLYING PROGRAM IN APR, MAY & JUNE 2020.Q1 TRAFFIC OF LESS THAN 150,000 PASSENGERS WILL BE 99.5% BEHIND Q1 BUDGET.RYANAIR - PLANS TO BE SUBJECT TO CONSULTATION BUT WILL AFFECT ALL RYANAIR AIRLINES, MAY RESULT IN LOSS OF UP TO 3,000 MAINLY PILOT AND CABIN CREW JOBS.OME RETURN TO FLIGHT SERVICES IS EXPECTED IN SECOND (JULY-SEPT) QUARTER,.RYANAIR EXPECTS TO CARRY NO MORE THAN 50% OF ITS ORIGINAL TRAFFIC TARGET OF 44.6M IN Q2.JOB CUTS AND PAY CUTS WILL ALSO BE EXTENDED TO HEAD OFFICE AND BACK OFFICE TEAMS.FOR FULL YEAR ENDED MARCH 2021, RYANAIR NOW EXPECTS TO CARRY LESS THAN 100M PASSENGERS,.WHEN SCHEDULED FLIGHTS RETURN IN EUROPE, SOMETIME IN JULY, RYANAIR BELIEVES IT WILL TAKE SOME TIME FOR PASSENGER VOLUMES TO RETURN..RYANAIR - GROUP CEO MICHAEL O'LEARY HAS NOW AGREED TO EXTEND THIS 50% PAY CUT FOR REMAINDER OF FINANCIAL YEAR TO MARCH 2021..EXPECTS TO REPORT A NET LOSS OF OVER EUR 100M IN Q1, WITH FURTHER LOSSES IN Q2."}
